//? Title: Trigram search: exact padded-byte Jaccard rankings
//? Subtitle: Actual native state, retained fixtures and explicit limits
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A misspelled query can fail exact string search. Comparing sets of short
substrings gives a simple fuzzy ranking, with an explicit choice of padding and
case folding.
)

\toc

> The method

Let A and B be distinct padded byte-trigram sets. J(A,B)=|A∩B|/(|A|+|B|−|A∩B|).
This lies in [0,1] because the intersection is contained in the union. Two empty
sets receive1. Repeated grams count once; this is set Jaccard rather than
occurrence-weighted similarity. Ranking is stable for equal scores.

> Simple worked example

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/trigram_search_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto aa = a::trigrams("cat"), bb = a::trigrams("bat");
    std::print("| word | actual padded grams |\n|---|---|\n|cat|`{}`|\n|bat|`{}`|\n\nActual Jaccard {}.\n",
               aa, bb, a::trigram_similarity("cat", "bat"));
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0},
                         std::format("cat: {} distinct grams", aa.size()));
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0},
                         std::format("bat: {} distinct grams", bb.size()));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0},
                         std::format("Actual Jaccard {}",
                                     a::trigram_similarity("cat", "bat")));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/trigram_search_tiny.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| word | actual padded grams |
|---|---|
|cat|`{"  c", " ca", "at ", "cat"}`|
|bat|`{"  b", " ba", "at ", "bat"}`|

Actual Jaccard 0.14285714285714285.
